  "ws_note": "Every 101 above is the PROXY accepting: its check passed, then websockets.connect to upstream raised InvalidStatus (56 'server rejected WebSocket connection' in proxy.log) because the websockets client sends the dot path as-is and marimo has no such route. So the WS check is bypassed but no shell was reached in these variants; HTTP is the exploitable path (httpx collapses dot segments after the check): 200 with the package list for /e/x/../api/packages/list, %2e%2e and ..%2f variants. POST variants got 401 'Missing server token' FROM MARIMO (reached it; a real author has the Marimo-Server-Token from the served page).",
  "phase": "before fix"
